ser":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:58:46-08:00","id":400280,"title":"","content":"Page 151, under &quot;Rites and Miracles.&quot; <br /> <br /> Ritualist characters may buy rites and miracles separately from the Ritual Discipline itself for two Experiences each. Every dot of Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery (including the first) also comes with a \u201cfree\u201d rite or miracle, taught by the covenant as part of ongoing training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:10:05-08:00","id":401956,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen costs if your using the Dynamic version of the system in Blood and Smoke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:14:12-08:00","id":401958,"title":"","content":"Well as written it should still be a flat 2 XP. However, I'd personally suggest lowering that to 1 for most weaker rituals <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:54:55-08:00","id":402363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/400051-cost-of-cruac-and-theban-rituals?p=401958#post401958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well as written it should still be a flat 2 XP. However, I'd personally suggest lowering that to 1 for most weaker rituals <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What if your buying themes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:11:42-08:00","id":402529,"title":"","content":"I use 2xp per Theme dot on my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:52:02-08:00","id":403058,"title":"","content":"Theme's were priced as In-Clan disciplines, so I'd say theme's should stay as in-clan (3 XP per Theme dot).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T03:48:47-07:00","id":680861,"title":"","content":"Can't find it anywhere, what's the XP cost of Theban/Cruac dots themself? 3XP? 4? The text implies that the cost for a rite is 2XP regardless of the dot rating of the rite. Is that right? Is there any limitation to the learning of the rites themselves? Can you learn a 4-dot rite with 2 dots in Cruac? If you buy a 3rd dot, do you get a 1- or 3-dot rite for &quot;free&quot;? The book is really bad at explaining this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:18:21-07:00","id":680878,"title":"","content":"When you get a new dot in Theban or Cruac, you're supposed to get the free ritual at the level you just purchased. If you're incapable of casting the ritual because it's at a level that exceeds your capability (the ritual is rated at 4 dots but your Cruac or Theban is only rated at level 2), how are you going to learn it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:19:51-07:00","id":680879,"title":"","content":"&quot;If you're incapable of casting the ritual because it's at a level that exceeds your capability (the ritual is rated at 4 dots but your Cruac or Theban is only rated at level 2)&quot;<br /> Where does it say this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:51:15-07:00","id":680898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/400051-cost-of-cruac-and-theban-rituals?p=680861#post680861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't find it anywhere, what's the XP cost of Theban/Cruac dots themself? 3XP? 4? The text implies that the cost for a rite is 2XP regardless of the dot rating of the rite. Is that right? Is there any limitation to the learning of the rites themselves? Can you learn a 4-dot rite with 2 dots in Cruac? If you buy a 3rd dot, do you get a 1- or 3-dot rite for &quot;free&quot;? The book is really bad at explaining this...</div> </div> </div> </div> The cost of purchasing Theban or Cruac is the same as an out of clan discipline. So 4 exp. <br /> <br /> Rites and miracles cost 2exp each, irregardless of level.<br /> <br /> Is there any limit? Nothing quite explicitly stated. However, its strongly implied (and going based on the previous edition and the work in the blood magic book, plus how vampire Disciplines in general work) you cannot cast a ritual that has a dot rating higher than your score in the ritual Discipline. As well, it just doesn't make logical sense for anyone to teach a ritual that you can't use. You don't run before you walk, after all. <br /> <br /> If you buy the third dot of Theban, nothing stops you from learning a 2nd dot rite. Technically, by the RAW, you could learn a 4th, but you can't cast it, and it makes little sense for you to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T05:10:05-07:00","id":680901,"title":"","content":"Most of that is how I thought it worked, just wanted to be absolutely sure. Pity it's so badly documented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T09:44:03-07:00","id":681055,"title":"","content":"While I'm the last person to say Blood and Smoke is clear or even very consistent with their rules applications, the standard WoD rule requiring you to possess respective pre-requisites before purchasing subsequent abilities is reiterated multiple times and in multiple books.<br /> <br /> <i>Merits marked as Style Merits allow access to specialized maneuvers. Each maneuver is a prerequisite for the next in its sequence. So if a Style Merit has a three-dot maneuver and a four-dot maneuver, you must purchase the three-dot version before accessing the four-dot. </i>(World of Darkness Rules Revisions p. 158)<br /> <br /> O<i>nly Acolytes in good standing (Circle of the Crone Status \u2022 or more) may learn Cr\u00faac or the rites that use it. If an Acolyte ritualist loses all status in the covenant, she may still use and develop the Discipline but not learn any more rites</i>. (Blood and Smoke p. 150)<br /> <br /> <i>A character may only learn rituals rated equal to or less than his dots in Cr\u00faac</i>. (Blood and Smoke p. 150)<br /> <br /> <i>Only priests of Lancea et Sanctum Status \u2022 or more may learn Theban Sorcery or miracles for use with it. If the ritualist loses all status in the covenant, he can no longer learn new miracles. Learning the Discipline entails oaths to never reveal its secrets to outsiders \u2014 and the church has miracles to find and enact vengeance upon oath-breakers.</i> <i>A character may only learn rituals rated equal to or less than his dots in Theban Sorcery.</i> (Blood and Smoke p. 150-151)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-28-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:29:55-07:00","id":682025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/400051-cost-of-cruac-and-theban-rituals?p=681055#post681055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>A character may only learn rituals rated equal to or less than his dots in Cr\u00faac</i></b>. (Blood and Smoke p. 150)<br /> <br /> <i>Only priests of Lancea et Sanctum Status \u2022 or more may learn Theban Sorcery or miracles for use with it. If the ritualist loses all status in the covenant, he can no longer learn new miracles. Learning the Discipline entails oaths to never reveal its secrets to outsiders \u2014 and the church has miracles to find and enact vengeance upon oath-breakers.</i> <i><b>A character may only learn rituals rated equal to or less than his dots in Theban Sorcery.</b></i> (Blood and Smoke p. 150-151)</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded parts are literally not in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:58:01-07:00","id":682060,"title":"","content":"Check to see if there is a downloadable update to your pdf file.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T08:27:32-07:00","id":682105,"title":"","content":"Looks like there is, thanks. I've been using an ancient copy of B&amp;S that I had lying around, forgot to update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}